**弱声明族**（需 `@feature enable type.weak`，*:
**Weak declarations** (needs `@feature enable type.weak`, **Rust only**):

- `@weakbind <contract> [<field body>]`: data stays in the tree, the library does not validate it; editors read the builtin contract;
- `@weakdata <name> { … }`: payload goes to a side table only, **never into the main tree** (same name: last wins);
- `@weakdoc <name>`: references a `.smlex` profile, **no payload block**, and the same profile cannot be attached twice.

All three are hints only: with or without them the parsed data tree is byte-identical. C / C++ / JS / Lua do not implement them (S9).

在当前块应用契约：校验字段类型/枚举/区间，并填充缺失字段的默认值。\\n\\n:
Apply a contract to the current block: validates field types/enums/ranges and fills in defaults for missing fields.

The contract must be defined before `@is`.

```sml
db {
    @is Server
    host: db1.internal
}
```

定义契约（schema），为块提供字段类型、枚举、默认值、区间约束。\\n\\n:
Define a contract (schema), providing field types, enums, defaults and range constraints for a block.

```sml
@contract Server {
    host: str
    port: int default 5432
}
```

The contract definition itself is not part of the parse result. `loose` is required to allow undeclared fields.
